# Files that run on the Linux server keep LF line endings however the
# repository is checked out or archived. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows
# default) git would otherwise hand them over as CRLF, and bash then chokes on
# the \r ending every line — install.sh dies with "invalid option name" before
# it has done anything, and the deploy silently does not happen.
*.sh       text eol=lf
*.service  text eol=lf
*.conf     text eol=lf
